From 4c6a424f63c81e133789dc137697ffc4beea8b53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:42:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(browser): reap named harness daemons whose owner died or
 went idle [daveey]

Named browser-harness daemons (browser_exec session=...) were spawned detached
(start_new_session) with no idle exit, and nothing stopped them when the owning
agent died: the atexit cleanup only reaches stop_harness_daemons when the legacy
_active_sessions cache is non-empty, which the CDP-override/local routes never
fill, and a SIGKILLed owner runs no atexit at all. 18 orphaned daemons (oldest
~5 days) were found under launchd on 2026-10-27, each holding a browser-level
CDP connection to the agent Chrome.

Each browser_exec on a named daemon now stamps
<harness runtime>/hermes-owners/<BU_NAME>/<pid>-<start>. reap_orphaned_harness_daemons
stops (via the harness's identity-checked --reload) every stamped daemon with no
live owner stamp, or idle past browser.harness_daemon_idle_s (default 7200 s).
It runs from browser_exec at most once a minute and at every process exit (after
dropping this process's own stamps). The shared "default" daemon is never
stamped or reaped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
